Title: make check-diff fails by default: IDH_HOME points at ~/.claude, scripts moved to ~/.agents
Created: 2026-11-12
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-11-12T10:02Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context
On padme, 2026-11-12, `make check-diff` on a clean checkout exits 2:
`python3: can't open file '/home/haduong/.claude/scripts/scoped-check.py'`.
`Makefile:21` sets `IDH_HOME ?= $(HOME)/.claude`. The harness scripts now
live under `~/.agents/scripts/`, and `~/.claude/scripts` does not exist.
With `IDH_HOME=$HOME/.agents` the target runs and passes (PR #661's gate).
AGENTS.md prescribes this command before every commit, so every lane hits it.
Cause not established past that: when the harness moved, and whether it
meant to leave a `~/.claude/scripts` link, are unknown.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `make check-diff` runs from a clean checkout with `IDH_HOME` unset
      (default fixed, or resolved via `$IDH_ROOT`)
- [ ] Every other `$(IDH_HOME)` use in the Makefile resolves too
- [ ] `make check-diff` green
